A||||5||mrfixit58||Door Skin Removal||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-08-2000||01:44 PM||||Hope one of you guys can help. I'm trying to remove a door skin. I've removed all the bolts on the sides, the pop rivits along the bottom, the clips holding the rods for the lock and door handle and, of course, the mirror. But, I still can't get the skin off. Does the dew wipe have to come off to reveal some hidden clip or screw? The skin is loose everywhere except along the top.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Help!!!<BR>Roy||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||07-08-2000||02:18 PM||||You might have to remove the dew wipe, but I don't think so.  (I just can't remember.)  Try lifting on the skin.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||07-08-2000||03:19 PM||||I tried lifting but that doesn't appear to be the answer. There seems to be a clip of some sorts next to the key lock but toward the mirror. It looks like it should unscrew but I'm not having any luck.<P>Any ideas would be appreciated.<P>Roy||||reg||13
Z||000003||TheFiero64||07-08-2000||04:29 PM||||There is 2 bolts behind the molding. You must unclip the molding from the inside. Be carefully the clips break very easily.<P>------------------<BR>Joshua Bumpus<BR>New Bedford, MA<BR><B>88 V6 + many more</B>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Sage||07-08-2000||04:30 PM||||You do have the trim off...right?  If not there is one 7mm screw under the long strip, and one phillips head on the short one (behind the handle) you may have to bend the lip a little to get at it, as this one goes in from the back of the door and the one under the long piece from the outside, then bend it back to reinstall.  If you've done this allready, I don't know.  As I recall, the dew wipes don't have to come off to remove the skin.  Its been a while since I had one off, but this is what I remember cause I didn't take pics.<P>Hope you get it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfixit58||07-08-2000||05:41 PM||||Thanks guys. I found the screws. The biggest pain was removing the two 11mm speed nuts that hold the handles on. And, as it turned out, the drivers door skin had been removed before so the screw by the door handle was missing.<P>Thanks again,<BR>Roy||||reg||1
